      "code": "G",
      "title": "Infinitive / gerund (want to, like doing)",
      "rule": "Baʼzi feʼllardan keyin *to + feʼl* keladi: *want, would like, need* — *I want to sleep.* (Men uxlashni xohlayman.) *We need to buy bread.* (Biz non sotib olishimiz kerak.) Baʼzi feʼllardan keyin *feʼl + -ing* keladi: *like, love, hate, enjoy* — *I like reading.* (Men oʻqishni yoqtiraman.) *Bekzod hates washing plates.* Bu juftliklarni yodlang: *want to, need to, would like to* — *like …ing, love …ing, hate …ing, enjoy …ing*.",
      "examples": [
        "I want to go home.",
        "Dilnoza would like to drink tea.",
        "We need to buy bread.",
        "Bekzod likes playing football.",
        "Hamida loves cooking.",
        "Aziz hates getting up early."
      ],
      "words": [
        { "en": "want to", "uz": "…ni xohlamoq" },
        { "en": "need to", "uz": "…ishi kerak" },
        { "en": "would like to", "uz": "…ni istamoq, …moqchi" },
